A||||6||My7Fieros||Hmmmmm.......cold start?||||1||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||01-10-2001||03:03 PM||||Is there a cold start injector on V6 model Fieros (88)? Reason I ask is my 88 runs fine, but seems to have a problem starting. Takes longer than it should (usually on first crank, but still NOTICABLY longer)and when it does crank, it idles VERY low and kinda "spits and sputters" for a few until it finally catches on....kinda like an old single engine airplane..."putt putt putt putt puttputtputtputt, varoom!"....my room mate always yells "CLEAR PROPS" everytime I start it lol! Anyway, could it be the cold start injector? Thanx........<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||01-10-2001||04:24 PM||||Off hand I'de have to say turn the CARB HEAT off and set your mixture to FULL RICH!  LOL!<P>Yes it has a cold start valve, it's located by the base of the distributor.<P>When was the last time you gave it a FULL tune-up? (ie: plugs, wires, cap, rotor and set timing?)||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||01-10-2001||05:59 PM||||I replaced the plugs, wires, battery, pick up coil, ignition control module, cap, and rotor just a couple of months ago. What could be the prob w/ the hard starting? (Yes the fuel pump "whines" for a couple of seconds before start up to).||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||01-10-2001||07:32 PM||||It might have a peice of dirt or other forign material in it. Then again, could just be bad. I don't know if there is a specific test for it or if you check it like the other injectors. Check in OGERS cave and see if he has a section about it.<BR>Have you got good fuel pressure? (My guess would be yes) It may just need a good upper-end cleaning.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||01-10-2001||09:28 PM||||Check base timing||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||01-11-2001||03:37 AM||||I thought they got rid of the cold start injector in 88...  Look for a fuel line and a fitting at the throttle body end of the fuel rail, that's the cold start injector.<P>I agree with Indiana, try running some fuel-system cleaner through there.||||reg||
Z||000006||Tom Philips||01-11-2001||08:50 AM||||The cold start injector only functions when the starter engages and the sensor measures a cold engine the source for the 12 volts to the cold start injector is on the starter solenoid (fusible link) check to see if when you have ignition switch in start position that you are getting 12 volts to the cold start injector (engine has to be cold) <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
